\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2 's Duhalde says  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  to help peso. \b0\par\par\uc2 155 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2002\par 14:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES, \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Feb 27 (Reuters) - Argentine President Eduardo Duhalde said on Wednesday the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would regain some of its value against the dollar whenever the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided on an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop it up. \par \par \uc2  "Whenever the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar will fall," Duhalde told local radio, in remarks that fell short of a direct call for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Argentine peso has fallen to 2.14/2.17 for large scale transactions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since a devaluation last month. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been pegged at one-to-one to the dollar for 10 years. \par \par \uc2  Duhalde has previously said that the ideal level for the peso would be 1.60/1.70 to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has carried out small \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days, but has failed to halt the peso's slide. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020227dy2r00psi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
