\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2 's Peso Closes Stronger On Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2002\par 22:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso closed slightly stronger Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Commercial banks quoted the peso closing at around ARS2.09 for interbank transactions after sliding earlier in the day to around ARS2.15 - at which point traders said  the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Tuesday the peso closed around ARS2.11. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $50 million in dollars, which would mark the largest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the peso began to float against the dollar earlier this month after being pegged 1:1 to the dollar for the past 11 years. \par \par \uc2  While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading desk confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it wouldn't confirm the amount of dollars sold. \par \par \uc2  Government-run Banco de la Nacion sold dollars for ARS2.15 and bought greenbacks for ARS2.05 Wednesday. As the country's largest bank, Nacion is often the government's key instrument to implement monetary policy, getting first dibs on dollars sold by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The peso rallied on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Asked who was purchasing the relatively ample supply of dollars from the  \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one trader replied: "Everyone." \par \par \uc2  Government officials have said they would like the peso to settle around ARS1.60-1.70 after an initial overshoot, and have made it clear they won't hesitate to use the country's reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary. \par \par \uc2  -By Dawn Weiner, Dow Jones Newswires; (5411) 4314-2757; dawn.weiner@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020227dy2r001d4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
