\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 3-Argentina woes spread to Uruguay via Banco Galicia. \b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2002\par 22:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Recasts lede; adds plan to return deposits, updates \par \par \uc2  stocks) \par \par \uc2  By Anahi Rama \par \par \uc2  MONTEVIDEO, Uruguay, Feb 13 (Reuters) - Argentina's financial woes on Wednesday spread to neighboring Uruguay, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed the local unit of Argentina's largest private bank for 90 days after a run on deposits. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Banco Galicia Uruguay SA - wholly controlled by \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Banco Galicia y Buenos Aires SA - and force a total suspension of activity for 90 days after the bank lost roughly a third of its deposits so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Officials from Uruguay's second-largest private bank said they may gradually return deposits in quotas or fixed-term deposits to clients, the vast majority of whom are Argentines seeking refuge from a devastating banking crisis at home. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the liquidity crunch resulted from a lack of confidence in Galicia due to problems at its banking \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Argentina, where many deposits have been frozen since December to keep local banks from collapsing in the wake of a traumatic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation in early January. \par \par \uc2  As shares in the group that controls Galicia fell, economists said Uruguay's banking system - widely seen as an foreign financial haven for Argentines - was still very stable but did face some limited danger of capital flight. \par \par \uc2  "For now, this is a lack of confidence specifically in the name Galicia rather than a systematic problem that could extend to other deposits in Uruguay," said Hernan Fardi, an analyst for the Maxinver.com consultancy in Buenos Aires. \par \par \uc2  "But there is a latent fear among Argentine depositors who may now pass their other deposits in Uruguay to the United States, for example," Fardi said. "So in that sense it's fair to say Argentina is having some contagion effect in Uruguay." \par \par \uc2  PROBLEMS ONLY AT GALICIA? \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said it would not force changes in Galicia Uruguay's management, but an auditor would be appointed to review the bank's finances. No financial assistance was expected to be provided, officials said. \par \par \uc2  The shares in Grupo Financiero Galicia , which controls Banco Galicia, shed 9 percent to 33.2 peso on the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange, as traders worried about the group's overall financial health, amid overall light gains. \par \par \uc2  A Galicia Uruguay source told Reuters on Tuesday that the run on deposits saw more than $300 million withdrawn in just five working days. Galicia Uruguay said in a statement it had deposits of $1.4 billion and a net worth of $231 million at the end of 2001. \par \par \uc2  The source also said GFG's banking \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Argentina were "very strong" thanks to the partial freeze in place on deposits to halt a run there amid a recession now in its fourth year. Ratings agencies, however, say that most of Argentina's banks are insolvent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the liquidity problem may also result from transfers by Galicia Uruguay to its Argentine headquarters. \par \par \uc2  But Uruguayan officials played down fears Argentina's problems could further affect banks in the mostly agricultural country, one of the few in Latin American to enjoy "investment grade" status from ratings agencies. \par \par \uc2  "Banks are strong," said Ramon Diaz, former president of Uruguay's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "This isn't going to even come close to spreading to the rest of the system." \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Banco Comercial, Uruguay's largest private bank, is under investigation by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to a separate judicial probe in Argentina of alleged illegal capital flight following the Argentine deposit freeze. \par \par \uc2  Concern over the investigation led its primary shareholders - J.P. Morgan Chase , Credit Suisse First Boston and Dresdner Bank - to announce their support for Banco Comercial last week. \par \par \uc2  (Additional reporting by Brian Winter in Buenos Aires). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020213dy2d00ukg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
