\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  shares firm, peso  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  continues. \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2002\par 23:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES, \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 29 (Reuters) - Argentine shares ended firmer on Tuesday amid arbitrage deals with the newly-devalued peso, which has been propped up almost daily by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The MerVal index ended 1.44 percent firmer at 425.10 points on turnover of 15.8 million pesos. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the peso closed at an average 1.77/1.80 per dollar for large-scale transactions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, slightly firmer from the previous close of 1.80/1.83. \par \par \uc2  The 1.80 peso sell rate is equivalent to a 44 percent decline from the pre-devaluation one-to-one peso-dollar rate that reigned for a decade. \par \par \uc2  "The stock market trended higher, tracking the dollar's trajectory," said Alfredo Ferrarini of Cohen brokerage. "The bourse and the dollar go hand in hand." \par \par \uc2  In local market action, Spanish-owned Banco Frances gained 25 centavos to 3.58 pesos, while steelmaker Acindar was 1 centavo firmer at 40 centavos. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the 11th straight session, selling U.S. dollars at 1.65 pesos to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Argentina also has an official fixed exchange rate of 1.40 pesos per dollar for foreign trade and priority transactions as designated by the government, and a floating peso for cash deals. The government has said it hopes to ditch the dual exchange rate and fully float the peso during the second half of the year. \par \par \uc2  The floating-rate peso has weakened as companies and the public alike have sought the safe haven of dollars due to fears that the peso will depreciate even further amid a deep recession now in its fourth year. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020129dy1t017dk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
