\par\par \b \uc2  Chile peso slides on Argentina woes. \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2002\par 20:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Chile, Jan 25 (Reuters) - Chile's peso slid on Friday, completing a week of volatile trade which is expected to continue while financial instability reigns in neighboring Argentina, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 671.50/672.00, a depreciation of 0.40 percent compared with 668.80/669.30. \par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate will continue to be volatile from here to March, fluctuating between 660 and 680 pesos," said Andres Perez, finance manager of BCI brokerage. \par \par \uc2  "The volatility will be due to the situation in Argentina, where they have announced first one measure, then another, then these are withdrawn. All this creates a lot of confusion and that has repercussions on the Brazilian real and the Chilean peso," Perez added. \par \par \uc2  Argentina devalued its peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  just over two weeks ago after a decade of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegged at one-to-one to the dollar. The devaluation has fuelled civil unrest and sent shock waves through regional markets. \par \par \uc2  Frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buoy the floating peso have contributed to doubts about the country's economic future. \par \par \uc2  Unlike other analysts, who expect Argentina's economic problems to smooth out after March, Perez says the political and social crises could worsen, bringing further problems for Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020125dy1p012fp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
