\par\par \b \uc2  Argentine peso up after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , stocks weak. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jorge A. Otaola \par \uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2002\par 16:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES, \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso strengthened on Wednesday as another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped keep prices stable despite jitters over a brutal financial crisis, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The stock market slumped 5 percent as traders took profits on some of the massive gains of the last two months. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the peso traded at an average 1.73/1.78 per dollar for large-scale transactions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, firmer than Tuesday's close of 1.80/1.85. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the seventh straight session, selling an unspecified amount of dollars at 1.62 to prop up the peso, the bank said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's participation has succeeded in controlling the dollar's offering price," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said the peso's value remained strong due to capital controls on banks that effectively reduce the amount of cash in circulation. \par \par \uc2  "Small savers continue trying to protect their assets by buying dollars in small quantities, but the banking curbs keep them from changing really large amounts," said a trader. \par \par \uc2  Argentina has an official fixed exchange rate of 1.40 pesos per dollar for foreign trade and priority transactions as designated by the government, and a floating peso for cash deals. The government hopes to ditch the dual exchange rate and fully float the peso during the second half of the year. \par \par \uc2  STOCKS WEAKER \par \par \uc2  Argentina's MerVal stocks index weakened 22 points to about 423 in brisk volume as traders sold off shares that ran up huge gains in December and January. \par \par \uc2  "The session looks just like yesterday, with sales in shares that did well after the government's decision to devalue," said a trader. \par \par \uc2  The market has backed off in the last two sessions but is up about 108 percent since Dec. 1. The rise came as savers snapped up hard property like jewelry, real estate and local shares on fears that cash in bank accounts could become worthless after a devaluation. \par \par \uc2  The peso was devalued by nearly 30 percent earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  Financial holding Grupo Financiero Galicia lost 8 percent to 66.5 centavos. Telecom Argentina shed 6.44 percent to 2.47 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Overall, 23 shares declined, four advanced and five were unchanged. Turnover was moderate at 3.9 million pesos. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020123dy1n00v6a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
