\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2 's Peso Closes 1.95/Dlr; Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  Again \b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2002\par 22:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso (ARS) held its ground Monday in thin trading resulting from the U.S. holiday and the country's partial banking freeze that is keeping larger companies from entering the local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which in the past week traders said has spent $50 million to $70 million selling dollars, kept the peso from losing ground. \par \par \uc2  Banks quoted the interbank midrate at ARS1.95 to the dollar, versus an open of ARS2.00 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  On Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses quoted the peso closing at a midrate of ARS1.93 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  As Argentina's peso has only been floating freely against the dollar since Jan. 11, banks have had to set up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. In the interim, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses were the primary source for peso prices. \par \par \uc2  While traders said the interbank market was technically \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2 , volume was scarce and there was still some confusion about trading. \par \par \uc2  "The interbank market is practically not operating," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with a locally based bank, referring to scarce volume. \par \par \uc2  Argentina's banking withdrawal restrictions, in place since early December, are making it difficult for large companies to participate in the market. "There is a scarcity of pesos," that is making the market more illiquid and keeping the price of the peso from weakening further, said the trader. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the country's financial institutions are having to build a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading system from scratch. Traders said there is still some confusion about market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued a communique asking \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses to submit detailed activity reports to the bank, as well as to tax agencies. \par \par \uc2  On the retail side, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses quoted the peso closing at a midrate of ARS1.75. \par \par \uc2  Retail peso sales have kept the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from further weakening. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses in downtown Buenos Aires had a steady flow of customers, anxious to sell dollars they had socked away under mattresses and in safety deposit boxes. Banking restrictions, which limit cash withdrawals to 1,500 pesos a month, are forcing them to sell the stored up greenbacks. \par \par \uc2  "I have to buy pesos to pay my bills," said one man standing in a two-block-long line outside a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  house on Florida Street, a busy downtown pedestrian walkway. A steady-flow of small volume customers seeking to buy pesos have kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from losing too much ground, traders said. \par \par \uc2  -By Dawn Weiner, Dow Jones Newswires; (5411) 4311-3127; argentina@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020121dy1l0019l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
