\par\par \b \uc2  Argentine cenbank sells dlrs in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  mkt at 1.75 pesos. \b0\par\par\uc2 188 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2002\par 20:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES, \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 17 (Reuters) - The Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the third straight day on Thursday, selling U.S. dollars at 1.75 pesos to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bank said. \par \par \uc2  The bank did not say how many dollars it sold. \par \par \uc2  Argentina has a dual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate - an official fixed rate of 1.40 pesos per dollar for foreign trade and preferred transactions as designated by the government, plus an unofficial floating peso for cash deals. \par \par \uc2  The floating-rate peso weakened sharply on Thursday as companies and people sought the safe haven of dollars on fears the peso might depreciate even further amid a deep recession now in its fourth year, traders said. \par \par \uc2  They said the peso traded at an average 1.90/1.95 per dollar for large-scale transactions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market immediately following news of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stronger than previous levels of 2.05/2.10. But the peso was still weaker than Wednesday's close at 1.83/1.87. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020117dy1h011nu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
