\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Real Ends Up On Invest,Bush's Argentina Aid Pledge \b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2002\par 20:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BRASILIA -(Dow Jones)- Brazil's real ended stronger Wednesday amid a boost from continued strong foreign investment inflows and a pledge from President Bush to work with the International Monetary Fund on assistance for Argentina. \par \par \uc2  The real ended at a midrate of BRR2.365 per dollar on a spread of BRR2.364 to BRR2.366. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at BRR2.375 per dollar Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "We've had more investment inflows than outflows and with hope for assistance in Argentina, the real saw a recovery," commented a trader in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  The real traded as low as BRR2.397 early in the session but then rebounded with the entrance of fresh investment and announcement of the U.S.' intentions to intensify aid efforts for Brazil's southern neighbor. \par \par \uc2  The market Wednesday reportedly saw proceeds from a large portion of a $100 million overseas debt offer by the local Votorantim group through Banco Santander. \par \par \uc2  Investors also took note of a market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the peso that should aid regional liquidity as well. \par \par \uc2  With more good news locally and renewed hope for a resolution to the Argentine crisis, traders here said they expected the real would continue to change hands at below the BRR2.40 per dollar mark in coming days. \par \par \uc2  -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-61-9965-6883; gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020116dy1g0018j\par }\page 