\par\par \b \uc2  Argentina's Peso Opens Unchanged At ARS1.85/Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2002\par 14:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso opened unchanged Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Tuesday to contain further weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  houses quoted the peso opening Wednesday at a midrate of ARS1.85 to the dollar. Spreads were ARS1.75 to ARS1.95 to the dollar, unchanged from Tuesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected $8.8 million into the new free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday, selling dollars at ARS1.7 as private banks covered positions. It was the first time the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected dollars into the market to contain further depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The peso has weakened 45.9% in just three sessions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar reached an intraday low of ARS2.05 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a move that pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to a midrate of ARS1.85 to the dollar just before \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets closed. \par \par \uc2  "We still don't see a clear direction on where the market is going," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. \par \par \uc2  Friday was the first day the peso floated freely against the dollar in nearly 11 years, as the government abandoned Argentina's convertibility policy, which pegged the peso to the dollar at a 1:1 ratio. \par \par \uc2  -By Dawn Weiner; Dow Jones Newswires; (5411) 4311-3127; argentina@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020116dy1g000t8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
