\par\par \b \uc2  Chile stocks close flat on Argentine peso jitters. \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2002\par 23:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Chile, Jan 15 (Reuters) - Chile's stocks closed flat on Tuesday, neutralizing important early gains after \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to break a steep fall in the neighboring country's new floated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  On the Santiago Stock Exchange, the index of the 40 top stocks rose 0.04 percent to 96.42 points while the general index slid 0.14 percent to 5,294.18 points. \par \par \uc2  In the morning, stocks recovered ground lost over recent days but could not hold these gains in the afternoon as nervous investors reacted to a decision by Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the peso, which had weakened to nearly 2.0 pesos to the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "The stocks held firm until the afternoon, buoyed up by purchases of key stocks at good prices. But nearly all these gains were lost due to the renewed turbulence in the Argentine economy," said Jorge Tolosa, analyst with Ugarte brokerage. \par \par \uc2  Argentina last week launched a dual exchange rate regime consisting of a fixed devalued peso of 1.40 per dollar and another floating peso. The floating rate is expected to converge with the fixed rate but has been highly volatile, obliging the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars on Tuesday at a rate of 1.70 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The day's stock market performance was a reminder to Chileans that its economy has not completely decoupled from the Argentine crisis, as stated by members of the government over recent weeks. \par \par \uc2  "This confirms the outlook that Argentina continues to be very fragile and could get worse. This is what the (Chilean) market interpreted it as and that led to the cutback in the gains," Tolosa said. \par \par \uc2  Among the heavyweights, energy group Enersis gained 1.36 percent to close at 149 pesos per share, while its distributor Endesa rose 2.21 percent to 208 pesos. \par \par \uc2  Copper manufacturer Madeco , which on Friday became the first Chilean company to scale back \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Argentina, lost 11.76 percent to 135.01 pesos, which resulted in the suspension of trading of its stocks. \par \par \uc2  ($1=663 pesos). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020115dy1f017ty\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
