\par\par \b \uc2  Chilean peso slips to new low on Argentine woes. \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2001\par 20:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Chile, Oct 5 (Reuters) - Chile's peso plunged to new historic lows on Friday on a worsening financial crisis in \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 709.90/710.10, a depreciation of 1.2 percent from the 701.40/701.70 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the day's trading was characterized by a high demand for dollars, especially from two multinational companies in the power and telecommunications sectors. \par \par \uc2  "The demand for dollars in the last two days has been so high that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not prevented further falls in the peso," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  According to a survey carried out by Reuters, the bank pumped $40 million into the market. The bank has now injected $410 million into the market since mid-August, when it broke with a two-year hands-off policy. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the financial problems in Argentina would continue to pressure the peso in the long term. \par \par \uc2  Argentina's chronic debt woes have also affected its principal trading partner Brazil, adding additional uncertainty to regional markets. \par \par \uc2  "I would expect the peso rates to hold in the short term due to the uncertainty over Argentina's economic future. At the same time I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should clarify its exchange rate policy," said Gabriela Clivio, analyst at Santiago brokerage. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba00