\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil real at new low close on Argentine fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2001\par 21:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, July 12 (Reuters) - Brazil's embattled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  chalked up its third new record low close in a row Thursday, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as players took a dim view of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest bid to pull itself out of the recessionary quagmire, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real weakened to 2.552 per dollar from Wednesday's previous record low close of 2.50 per dollar, leaving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly 31 percent below where it began the year. Earlier it hit a new record intraday level of 2.58 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The new historic close came despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's seventh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market this month. Traders say the bank has sold some $50 million to bolster the real in each of the last six sessions. \par \par \uc2  The real plunged this week as a fresh wave of fears of Argentine fiscal insolvency and debt default swept through the market, adding to existing concerns about the impact of the U.S. economic slowdown and local energy shortage crisis. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Argentine government's latest pledge late Wednesday to eliminate the budget gap for the rest of the year by cutting spending and fighting tax evasion had done little to lift the cloud of over the neighboring economy. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx7c026pj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
