\par\par \b \uc2  Peru's Toledo says secures Congress support-analyst. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hugh Bronstein \par \uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2001\par 18:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, April 26 (Reuters) - Leading Peruvian presidential candidate Alejandro Toledo told Wall Street economists on Thursday that he has negotiated majority support for his economic reforms in Congress, a development that would improve his prospects for reviving economic growth, a participant in the meeting said. \par \par \uc2  "He told us today that he has undergone negotiations to assure a majority in Congress with other parties if he were to be elected, " Miguel Palomino, chief economist for Latin America at Merrill Lynch, told Reuters after the meeting. \par \par \uc2  "This is positive in that it implies significantly improved governability," Palomino said. \par \par \uc2  It was not immediately clear with whom Toledo could have struck a deal. His Peru Posible will be the biggest force in the new Congress, but has no majority. The next biggest is the American Popular Revolutionary Alliance (APRA) of his rival in the upcoming runoff election, ex-president Alan Garcia. \par \par \uc2  Whoever wins the runoff - likely to occur on June 3 - is likely to have to strike a deal with the Unidad Nacional (National Unity) party of defeated first-round contender Lourdes Flores or the Independent Moralizing Front (FIM) of ex-legislator Fernando Olivera. Peruvian analysts see much of Flores' support going to Garcia. \par \par \uc2  The first round of voting for president was on April 8, the same day the new Congress was elected. The incoming legislature will hold its first session on July 27, one day before the new president is due to take office. \par \par \uc2  Toledo, a former World Bank economist, was in New York to sell his economic program to analysts who have been concerned that the campaign is drifting in a fiscally irresponsible direction as Toledo and Garcia compete for votes. \par \par \uc2  "I AM NOT A POPULIST," TOLEDO SAYS \par \par \uc2  His message was summed up in a brief statement he made to reporters between meetings when he said, "No soy un populista," or "I am not a populist." \par \par \uc2  JP Morgan sovereign debt strategist Luis Oganes said Toledo was convincing. \par \par \uc2  "We all know Mr. Toledo is facing a very populist candidate and that the second round campaign could become a war of populist ideas," Oganes said. \par \par \uc2  One concern voiced recently by Wall Street was that Toledo had proposed a series of tax cuts intended to boost consumption. \par \par \uc2  "But he stressed and clarified that fiscal discipline would not be sacrificed at the expense of trying to promote consumption by way of tax cuts," Oganes said. "That was an important message for us." \par \par \uc2  Peru's economy has declined this year amid political turmoil left in the wake of former President Alberto Fujimori, who fled to Japan late last year after being fired amid a bribery scandal centering on his former intelligence chief. \par \par \uc2  Interim Economy Minister Javier Silva Ruete has trimmed Peru's gross domestic product (GDP) forecast for 2001 to 1-2 percent from a target set with the International Monetary Fund of 2-3 percent, a ministry spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  Peru's sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank through a psychological level of 3.6 to the dollar on Wednesday, a fresh historic low, before recovering on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a confidence crisis in \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that has affected regional markets. \par \par \uc2  Toledo, a centrist free-marketeer with leftist rhetoric, finished first in the April 8 elections but failed to secure the outright majority he predicted and was forced into a runoff by Garcia, whose 1985-90 government left Peru in economic chaos. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4q0176q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
47
