\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela/Defy Odds/Devaluation -4: International Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1998\par 00:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Internationally, Brady bonds and American depositary receipts trading in New York took a nosedive Thursday, and markets from Mexico to Argentina plunged. \par \par \uc2  Analysts fear that a messy bolivar devaluation will be the final blow for much-abused investors in emerging markets, and could put undue pressure on other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Brazilian real and the Mexican peso. \par \par \uc2  "If the bolivar goes the Brazilian real will go next and that will pull Argentina and the rest of Latin America with it," said Marcelo Simini, fund manager for investment bank Merchant Bankers Asociados SA in Buenos Aires. \par \par \uc2  Others were slightly more optimistic on damage control. "If Venezuela devalues there will be a lot of pressure to devalue in Brazil. But Brazil plays hard ball and I think it will resist the pressure," said Roger Heal, an analyst at West Merchant Bank Ltd in Buenos Aires. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico, the key IPC index fell 2.9% to 3498.81 while the peso closed at a record low of a midrate of 9.3450 pesos to the dollar from 9.1970 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  For Mexico, there's an additional concern: the possibility that Venezuela's deteriorating economic outlook could undermine the country's commitment to reduce crude exports in a joint effort with Mexico and Saudi Arabia aimed at boosting world oil prices. \par \par \uc2  In Brazil, the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's Bovespa index fell to a nine-month low, closing 6.4% lower at 7991, while the real finished flat - thanks to apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Merval index dropped 6.1% to 441.83. In Chile, the peso ended at 472.40 pesos to the dollar from 471.90 the previous day, while the IPSA stock index shed 3.9%. \par \par \uc2  Venezuelan Brady bonds were pummeled in New York. The country's Pars fell 6 1/2 to 59 bid, while the DCBs plummeted 12 5/8 points to 46 7/8 bid. \par \par \uc2  Venezuela's benchmark ADR, CANTV, dropped 13% to close at 14 3/4. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-08-98 \par \par \uc2  2213GMT \par \par \uc2  1191 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8k0742k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
