\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2 's Peso Weakens Off Ceiling; No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1995\par 20:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUENOS AIRES (AP-DJ)--The Argentine peso weakened moderately against the U.S. dollar on Thursday, allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the first time in weeks, a spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  The peso was trading at 0.9987 peso to the dollar, compared to 0.9980 peso on Wednesday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a hefty 48.4 million dlrs. \par \par \uc2  Despite the slight weakening, liquidity levels remained tight and interbank interest rates inched higher. The overnight rate on peso-denominated loans between first-line banks, or call money, jumped to 23% from 22% on Wednesday. Call money in dollars held stable at 8.5%. \par \par \uc2  The peso had slumped to its floor on the dollar after Mexico decided to devalue and then free float its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But one Buenos Aires trader said that the demand for the peso this week came from second-line banks covering their minimum cash reserve requirements with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The reserve accounting period ends Jan. 15. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't renew any securities repurchase tenders, the spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-01-95 \par \par \uc2  1915GMT \par \par \uc2  1157 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr150031i\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\br